# Residual CVEs in the Google-supplied deployer_helm base image.
#
# These live in binaries and packages Google builds and ships. Nothing in this
# repository installs, compiles or vendors them, so they cannot be remediated
# here. See the design spec, 2.6/2.7.
#
# REVIEW THIS FILE AT EVERY BASE BUMP. Delete any entry the new base has fixed.
# A stale ignore is indistinguishable from a missing gate.
#
# Re-derived 2026-11-05 against base sha256:142cee99 (helm 4.3.1 / kubectl
# 1.37.2). The previous set was derived against sha256:dab57d60; that bump
# cleared CVE-2026-78663, CVE-2026-56857 and CVE-2026-111497, all three flagged
# by Marketplace validation on 2026-11-05. Findings 11 -> 6.
#
# Track record of base bumps and ignore turnover:
#   6a6d7059 (09-09) -> 14 entries
#   dab57d60 (10-26) ->  9 entries, ZERO overlap with the previous set
#   142cee99 (11-05) ->  6 entries
# Carrying ignores forward across a bump is therefore always wrong.
#
# SCOPE LIMIT -- READ BEFORE TRUSTING A PASSING GATE.
# This gate runs at --severity HIGH,CRITICAL. It is NOT the image's total
# finding count, and it does not match Google's scanner coverage: Artifact
# Registry has reported CVEs this scanner did not carry, and rates some
# findings differently. A pass means "no new HIGH/CRITICAL that we know of and
# have not excused" -- nothing stronger.


